tempered (3.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * TEMPerHUM support (same USB ID 3553:a001, firmware TEMPerHUM_*):
    the daemon presents its temperature and relative humidity as two
    IIO devices, linked as /run/tempered/temperature and
    /run/tempered/humidity (TEMPERED_HUMIDITY_LABEL).  Needs the
    kernel's hid-sensor-humidity.  One stick at a time: the daemon
    refuses to start beside another HID temperature or humidity
    sensor until the kernel fix in patches/ lands.
  * tempered read prints "C %RH" for a TEMPerHUM; info adds the model
    and humidity; log adds humidity_percent and drops centi_celsius.
  * Library (tempered-hid), breaking: values are Celsius and
    RelativeHumidityPercent in natural units, replacing CentiCelsius,
    DeciCelsius and DeciPercent; Stick::reading() replaces
    Stick::temperature() and reports humidity for models that have
    it.  New: Model, Firmware::model(), Stick::model().
  * The TEMPerGold's IIO device is unchanged.

 -- Christopher Hoover <ch@murgatroid.com>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 20:59:20 -0700

tempered (2.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Security: lock files under /run/tempered are now private (0600).
    Before, any local user could take the label's lock and keep the
    daemon from starting.
  * Requires systemd 253 or later (for OpenFile=), now a package
    dependency: Debian trixie or Ubuntu 24.04, not bookworm.
  * A stick with other firmware on the same USB ID, such as a TEMPerHUM
    or TEMPer2, is refused with exit status 3 instead of restarting in
    a loop.  The firmware query is retried at startup, for sticks slow
    to answer after plug-in.
  * The daemon refuses to start beside another HID temperature sensor
    (the kernel's hid-sensor-temperature mishandles two and can oops);
    one left by a crashed instance gets 10 s to go away.  Kernel fixes
    are in patches/ and have been sent upstream.
  * The held reading's age counts time spent suspended, SIGHUP shuts
    the daemon down cleanly, and a shutdown during startup keeps its
    exit status.
  * The virtual HID sensor's descriptor uses an Application collection
    and a 32-bit temperature field, so buffered IIO reads of negative
    temperatures are right.
  * The suspend hook no longer blocks resume, and restarts only
    daemons whose stick is still there.  Reinstalling starts the daemon
    for a stick already plugged in.  Purging locks the tempered account
    instead of deleting it.
  * The tempered-hid library's API changes (2.0): opening a stick
    returns hidraw::Error, which names the node on failure; error
    variants are non_exhaustive.  Additions include VENDOR_ID and
    PRODUCT_ID, constructors for the value types, Stick::into_inner,
    and AsFd for Hidraw.  The stick gets 1 s to settle after opening
    and 20 ms before each command, as PCsensor's own software does.
  * tempered read, info and log no longer repeat the device name in
    errors.

 -- Christopher Hoover <ch@murgatroid.com>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 18:17:53 -0700

tempered (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * First release.  tempered presents a PCsensor TEMPerGold USB
    thermometer (3553:a001) as a Linux IIO device: tempered daemon reads
    the stick over hidraw and creates a virtual HID sensor through
    /dev/uhid, which the kernel's HID sensor drivers turn into an
    ordinary iio:deviceN, linked as /run/tempered/<label>.
  * udev starts tempered@hidrawN when the stick is plugged in and stops
    it when it is unplugged; the stick's keyboard interface is
    deauthorized so it cannot type readings into a console.
  * The last reading is held for 60 s (TEMPERED_HOLD) once the stick
    stops answering; after that the IIO device is removed, so readers
    see the failure rather than a stale value.
  * The daemon refuses to start if another HID temperature sensor
    exists: the kernel's hid-sensor-temperature cannot handle two.
  * tempered read, info and log (JSON Lines) read the stick directly,
    with the daemon stopped.
  * The tempered-hid library, MIT OR Apache-2.0, is on crates.io.

 -- Christopher Hoover <ch@murgatroid.com>  Tue, 06 Oct 2026 20:48:33 -0700
